hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1459","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told me, Abdul Razzaq told me, Ibn Jurayj told me, Ata told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I heard him. He says: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “rose on the Day of Fitr, and began to pray before the sermon, then he addressed the people. When the Prophet of God finished, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He descended and went to the women and reminded them. He was leaning on Bilal’s hand, and Bilal was spreading his garment, giving the women charity. I said For giving: Zakat on the Day of Fitr? He said: “No, but it is charity to be given in charity at that time. The woman throws her semen, and they throw it away.” I said to Ataa: Do you think it is right for the imam to come now? When he finishes with women, does he remind them? He said: “That is, by my life, this is a duty upon them, and why should they not do that?”"
"1460","Abu Bakr said: And in the news of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded them to By fearing God, he advised them and reminded them, and he praised and praised God, and urged them to obey Him, then he said: “Give alms; Indeed, the most of you is the firewood of Hell.” A woman from among the women with blond cheeks said: Why, O Messenger of God? He said: “You are so many.” They complained, and the family became infidels, so they started donating their necklaces, jewelry, earrings, and rings, throwing them onto Bilal’s clothing to give them in charity.” It was narrated by Bundar, it was narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, it was narrated by Abu Kurayb, it was narrated to us by Muhammad bin Bishr, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn My father Suleiman"
